Short:        COBOL and the Year 2000
Author:       Andreas R. Kleinert
Uploader:     Andreas_Kleinert t-online de
Type:         dev/src
Architecture: m68k-amigaos

 You can read various interesting texts and tutorials
 about the Year 2000 problem, software only using
 two-digit variables for their year counter, etc.

 But did you ever take a look at a real COBOL source
 code that deals with date checking ?

 Here's one - and it's Y2K (2000/2100) proof.
 Hopefully ;)

 datpruef.cbl:  - the original german version
 datcheck.cbl:  - the english translation

 --
 ARK, 02/Jan/99
